{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And seven days were fulfilled.</b> Rashi explained: such was the way of all the plagues — each one lasted a quarter of a month, and for the three parts he would warn him; thus the plague together with the warning was a full month. As it is written: ״שלח אותות ומופתים בתוככי מצרים״ — where he could have written בתוך, the letters כי are extra, which total thirty; thus a full month. However, it is difficult for me, for according to this interpretation it implies there were only twenty-eight days. And one may say: after the day of the plague he would wait until twenty-eight [days]. However, this too is difficult, for darkness lasted only six days, as it is written ״שלשת ימים״ and additionally three others during which ״לא קמו איש מתחתיו״. And one may say: this refers to the darkness that was over the Sea of Suph, as it is written ״ויהי הענן והחשך״ — that darkness completed it to seven. And it is stated in the Haggadah of Passover: Rabbi Yehudah would give signs for them: דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב. And they ask: what difference does this sign make? And R. Yitzchak bar R. Asher — who was born on the day R. Yitzchak bar Asher, of blessed memory, died, and they named him after him, and applied to him the verse ״וזרח השמש ובא השמש״ — explains: this is why this sign exists: for when you place דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב one upon the other, you find in every respect — at the beginning, in the middle, and at the end — darkness, boils, lice — to say that all three serve as one. But it was not explained how. And also you find that darkness is the reverse — and he would say that darkness serves with all of them. And also when you place חשך שחין כנים, you find in each, at the beginning and at the end: darkness, boils, lice — to say that all three are intermingled with the others. But it was not explained how. And yet one may further say: this is why he gave a sign for them — to inform that in this order they occurred, not in the order written in the book of Psalms. Or alternatively, to know regarding which he would warn and regarding which he would not warn, for in every third plague he would never warn, as we say: one who was punished and repeated — they imprison him in a cell and feed him barley until his stomach bursts." "<b>After HaShem struck the river.</b> Therefore the river first, because the Egyptians worshipped the river, for its waters are blessed. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: I will strike his god before him, and afterwards him. And likewise the parable: ״מחי אלהיא ויתבהלון כומרייא״ — when the god is struck, the priests panic."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The unvocalized abbreviations דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב are the standard mnemonics for the ten plagues; resolved here mechanically by context. The verse from Ecclesiastes (1:5) is referenced in unvocalized form and rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:00.445234340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}